• New: NTFS (Windows) drives read and write, plain or inside VeraCrypt/LUKS
• New: BitLocker drives unlock with their password or recovery key
• New: Mac APFS drives open read-only, plain or encrypted
• New: NTFS drives Windows did not shut down cleanly open read-only, keeping its pending changes safe
• New: Folder access given to other apps (e.g. Backup Master) survives remounts
• Known limitation: Windows-compressed NTFS files are read-only; EFS-encrypted files cannot be opened
